Is it really when you turn it off, or when you turn it back on?
If its when you turn it back on, check for garbage in the "hereis" message in
the terminal.  In either case check for noise from the terminal during power
cycle.

Something from the terminal is being interpretted by the VAX. 

>A coworker says that she thinks that is standard behavior for VAXens.  Even if
>it is, I would like to change this behavior if possible. Does anyone know of
>any way to alter this behavior.
> 

None of my VAXen have ever rebooted in response to a DEC VT terminal being
cycled.  I have had problems with cheap terminal clones generating what
looked like "break" during power on or off, but I never tried to use on of
those as a VAX console.

