I have a VS3100 38 and a VT420 terminal that DOES cause the VS3100 to reboot
after turning the VT420 off and on.  I have heard this happen to other people
with simular setups (all DEC hardware no pc vt emulations or pc vax emulations).

A way around this is to hook up the console port to a DS200 (with the latest
down line load software, previous versions did transmit break).  Although I have
not done this (I plan to as soon as I have a spare second or two) I know someone
who has and they report that it works great.  Of course this means you need a
DS200 with a spare port.... :-)

